-- title:
--   Diagonal descent of T_ℓ (ℓ≠ p) to the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Arithmetic data. A prime $p$ and an integer $M$ with $5\le M$ and $p\nmid M$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ of type $\{p\}$, together with $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity; an intermediate field $K$ of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with $K=$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-algebra generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb Q$; a discrete valuation ring $A$ which is a domain with $L$ as fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$; an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that of $L$; and an element $j\in K$ whose underlying Laurent series is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), with $j\neq 0$. All that follows concerns the two-chart integral model [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A (↥K) j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) over $\operatorname{Spec}A$, written $X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$ below, which is moreover assumed proper.
--
--   Special fibre. An algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $p$ which is an $A$-algebra; two schemes $C_1,C_2$ with structure morphisms $c_1,c_2$ to $\operatorname{Spec}k$, each proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral; closed immersions $i_1,i_2$ of $C_1,C_2$ into the base change $X_k$, compatible with the structure morphisms; the hypothesis `hcover`, that every point of $X_k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$; the hypothesis `hred`, that the scheme-theoretic intersection $\mathrm{pullback}\,i_1\,i_2$ is reduced; and a natural number $n$ with `hn`, `hn0`, asserting that this intersection has exactly $n$ points and $0<n$.
--
--   Sections. A section $\varepsilon$ of $X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$, sections $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2$ of $c_1,c_2$, and `hε₁`, requiring that $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ is the base change of $\varepsilon$ to $k$.
--
--   Relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ data. A designation $D$ for $X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$, that is a scheme $D.P$ with a structure morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec}A$ and a zero section; `hrep`, the (nonempty) datum of a representation `RepresentsRelSubPic` of the sub-Picard functor cut out by `algEquivZeroCut`, whose predicate is `FibrewiseAlgEquivZero`: a Poincaré rigidified line bundle on $X\times_A D.\mathrm{toBase}$ satisfying that predicate, the universal property that every rigidified line bundle with that property over a base $T$ is induced by a unique $T$-point of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$, and triviality along the zero section; and `hsm`, `hsep`, that $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is smooth and separated. Further: `hreps`, a representation of the same kind for the base change of $X$ and of $D$ to $k$; `hPk`, an isomorphism of its Poincaré bundle with the one obtained from `hrep` by base change; designations $D_1,D_2$ for $c_1,c_2$ with representations `hrep₁`, `hrep₂` relative to $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2$; and a morphism $\nu_2$ from $(D\otimes k).\mathrm{toBase}$ to $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}k$, characterised by `hν₂`: for every $t\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ and every $T$-point $a$ of $(D\otimes k).\mathrm{toBase}$, the Poincaré bundle of $D_2$ pulled back along $a$ followed by $\nu_2$ is isomorphic to the rigidification, along `rigSection c₂ t ε₂` and $\mathrm{pr}_2$, of the pull-back along `curveChange i₂.1 i₂.2 t` of the bundle classified by $a$; thus $\nu_2$ is pull-back of line bundles along $i_2$.
--
--   Behaviour over $L$ and over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Algebra structures making $A\to L\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ a tower into `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`; `hsmL`, `hgiL`, that $X_L$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral; `hprL`, `hgcL`, that $\mathrm{pr}_2\colon D.P\times_A L\to\operatorname{Spec}L$ is proper and geometrically connected.
--
--   Generic fibre curve model. A `CurveModel` $M_\eta$ over `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` for the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) — a proper smooth integral curve with a fixed isomorphism of its function field with that field, a bijection between its closed points and the places, and the attendant compatibilities — an isomorphism $e_\eta$ from $M_\eta.C$ to $X_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}$ with `heη` expressing compatibility over the base; a nonemptiness assumption on the preimage of the finite chart; `hMηpin`, that for every element $a$ of the finite chart algebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A (↥K) j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135), the function-field element obtained from $a$ through $e_\eta$ and the germ map has Laurent expansion the image of that of $a$ under [`ModularCurve.coeffMap`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L16) of $L\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and `hgal`, that for every $\mathbb Q$-automorphism $g$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ fixing $L$ pointwise and all $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points $x,x'$ of $M_\eta.C$ whose images in $X_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}$ satisfy $x'=g^{*}x$, the place attached to $x'$ is the translate of the place attached to $x$ by [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) of $g$.
--
--   Hecke and diamond inputs. `hin : ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsAll (M * p)` and `hcomm : ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondCommuteBar (M * p)`, the latter stating that the diamond generators over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ commute pairwise.
--
--   Galois action on $A$. A multiplicative semiring action of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb Q)$ on $A$ and `hΓA`, that $A\to L$ is equivariant for it.
--
--   Special fibre group data. An object $G$ of [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9): abelian groups $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$, a subgroup $G.\mathrm{torus}$ of $G.J0s$, and a surjective homomorphism $G.\mathrm{proj}\colon G.J0s\to G.JI\times G.JE$ with kernel $G.\mathrm{torus}$. Bijections $\mathrm{pts}$, $\mathrm{ptsI}$, $\mathrm{ptsE}$ of $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$ with the $k$-points of $(D\otimes k).\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_1.\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$; `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE`, that each bijection turns addition into the tensor product of the corresponding pull-backs of the relevant Poincaré bundle; and `hproj`, that the two components of $G.\mathrm{proj}\,x$ correspond under $\mathrm{ptsI}$, $\mathrm{ptsE}$ to post-composition of $\mathrm{pts}\,x$ with `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom` along $i_1$ and with $\nu_2$ respectively.
--
--   Operators on $D$ and $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points. A bijection $\mathrm{gpts}$ between [`ModularCurve.JOne (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$; a map $\varphi$ from [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlgOne`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L16) $=\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Primes}\oplus\mathbb N)\,\mathbb Z$ to endomorphisms of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}A$; and for each $s\in\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb Q)$ a morphism $\tau(s)$ of $D.P$ semilinear over the automorphism of $A$ given by $s$. The compatibilities are: `hφmul`, each $\varphi(t)$ is a homomorphism for the relative group law supplied by `hrep` through `algEquivZeroGroupCut`; `hφpts`, for the module structure [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleOneBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L129), $\mathrm{gpts}(t\cdot x)$ is $\mathrm{gpts}(x)$ followed by $\varphi(t)$; `hτ1` and `hτmul`, that $\tau(1)$ is the identity and $\tau(ss')$ is $\tau(s)$ followed by $\tau(s')$; `hτφ`, that $\tau(s)$ and $\varphi(t)$ commute; `hgadd`, that $\mathrm{gpts}$ is additive for the relative group law; and `hτpts`, that for $\sigma'$ on $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ restricting to $s$ on $L$ one has $\mathrm{gpts}(\sigma'\cdot x)=\operatorname{Spec}(\sigma')$ followed by $\mathrm{gpts}(x)$ followed by $\tau(s^{-1})$.
--
--   Abel–Jacobi data. A representation `hDL` over $L$ for the base changes of $X$ and $D$; a morphism $\mathrm{ajL}$ from $X_L$ to $(D\otimes L).\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}L$; a morphism $\mathrm{kL}$ from $X_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}$ to $X_L$; a morphism $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ from $M_\eta.C$ to $D.P$; a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-point $\overline\varepsilon$ of $M_\eta.C$; `hPL`, an isomorphism of the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` with the one obtained by base change from `hrep`; `hajLε`, that $\mathrm{ajL}$ carries the base-changed section $\varepsilon$ to the zero section; `hajL`, the Abel–Jacobi property: for every field $K'$, every $K'$-point of $\operatorname{Spec}L$ and every point $x$ of $X_L$ above it, the bundle classified by $x$ followed by $\mathrm{ajL}$ is isomorphic to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of the section, that is to $\mathcal O(x-\varepsilon)$; `hkL₁`, `hkL₂`, the two compatibilities of $\mathrm{kL}$ with the projections; `hajbar`, defining $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ as $e_\eta$, then $\mathrm{kL}$, then $\mathrm{ajL}$, then the first projection, with `hajbar_over` its compatibility over the base; `hεbar`, that $\overline\varepsilon$ maps to $\varepsilon$; `hεbar_aj`, that $\overline\varepsilon$ followed by $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ is the zero section over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and `hpts_aj`, that for all $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points $x,s$ of $M_\eta.C$ with $s$ mapping to $\varepsilon$ there is a degree-zero divisor $Dv$ equal to $[\,\text{place of }x\,]-[\,\text{place of }s\,]$ whose class satisfies $\mathrm{gpts}(Dv)=x$ followed by $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$.
--
--   Conclusion. For every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\neq p$ there exist endomorphisms $u_1$ of $D_1.\mathrm{toBase}$ and $u_2$ of $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$, each over $\operatorname{Spec}k$, such that the following three assertions hold.
--
--   First, for every commutative $k$-algebra $T'$ and all $T'$-points $v,v'$ of $(D\otimes k).\mathrm{toBase}$ (sections over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $k\to T'$) such that $v'$ followed by the projection $\mathrm{pr}_1\colon D.P\times_A k\to D.P$ equals $v$ followed by that projection and then by $\varphi(\,$[`ModularCurve.heckeGenOne ⟨ℓ, hℓ⟩`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L18)$\,)$, the polynomial generator of `HeckeAlgOne` indexed by $\ell$: the post-composition of $v'$ with `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom` along $i_1$ equals the post-composition with $u_1$ of the post-composition of $v$ with that same map, and the post-composition of $v'$ with $\nu_2$ equals the post-composition with $u_2$ of the post-composition of $v$ with $\nu_2$.
--
--   Second, $u_1$ is a homomorphism for the relative group law of $D_1$ attached to `hrep₁` through `algEquivZeroGroupCut`: for every $s\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ and all $T$-points $x,y$ of $D_1.\mathrm{toBase}$, the composition of the product $x\cdot y$ with $u_1$ equals the product of the compositions of $x$ and of $y$ with $u_1$.
--
--   Third, the same assertion for $u_2$ and the relative group law of $D_2$ attached to `hrep₂`.
--
--   This is the diagonal descent, for primes $\ell\neq p$, of the Hecke endomorphism $T_\ell$ of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the valuation ring $A$ of $\mathbb Q(\zeta_p)$ above $p$: the operator induced on each of the Jacobians $D_1,D_2$ of the two components $C_1,C_2$ of the special fibre over $\overline{\mathbb F}_p$, compatibly with the pull-back maps $\pi_1$ along $i_1$ and $\pi_2=\nu_2$ along $i_2$. It is consumed by the assembly of the special-fibre operator package for the model of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$, where it supplies the $\ell\neq p$ part of the Hecke action used in the level-lowering argument.
